From c31cb64773e420e6fc008acfd55c146bd71cd4d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:22:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plate): PLATE-01 - a specular return cannot exceed the
 light that arrives
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found by running the preview in a real browser rather than in a test harness.
The component in DESIGN-01 had never executed: it is a canvas, a ResizeObserver
and a banded render loop, and none of that runs under vitest. Compiled it,
served it, and drove it with Chromium — six species, real webp decode, the same
banding the component does. It works, at 52 to 113 milliseconds a plate at
420x315 in V8, which is what the banding exists to spread across frames.

It also showed maple and white ash washing out, and the measurement named it.
The sheen was ADDED: a fixed lift scaled by the finish and the grazing angle.
That is fine on walnut, which has headroom, and ruinous on a pale floor, which
does not. White ash lost 0.45% of its floor to pure white and read as a flat
bright field with the wood washed out of it.

Screening instead — adding a fraction of the REMAINING headroom — cannot exceed
white by construction. Measured over the near two-thirds of the frame:

                  clipped to white      near-field detail
    white ash     0.45%  ->  0.00%      6.25  ->  6.46
    hard maple    0.00%  ->  0.00%      4.67  ->  4.75
    white oak     0.00%  ->  0.00%      6.09  ->  5.80
    black walnut  0.00%  ->  0.00%      4.72  ->  4.51

The clipping is gone and the palest two species keep more figure. The two
darker ones lose a little measured neighbour-delta and about four percent of
their brightness, which is the screen doing what a screen does: it adds less
where the surface is already bright. Side by side across all six it reads
richer, not darker — white oak shows more board definition and hickory's
herringbone separates better.

Raising the coefficient does not undo the darkening (0.62 to 0.92 moves the
mean by two levels out of 255 and costs detail) because the darkening is not a
coefficient, it is the model. 0.62 measured best and is what ships.

It is also the better physical model, which is the reason to keep it even where
it costs a little: a specular return is light the surface sends back, and a
surface cannot send back more than arrives.

Also: grainTextureFor in floor-assembly.ts composed the tile URL from a string
template, which is a second definition of a path that
scripts/textures/build-grain.py already writes into the tile table. A template
can name a file that does not exist, and the failure is not an exception — it
is a 404 and a floor that paints as flat brown and still looks deliberate. I
saw exactly that while building the browser harness and spent a minute
believing it was the site. It delegates now. The existing test still asserts
the same path and the same file on disk, unchanged, because the answer is the
same answer.

65 of 66 guards. parse-scan clean on 641 files. Both service test files pass.

